label Siren
if {done} == true:
	siren: Do you see that pile of metal behind you? Pick up as many as you can, and bring them over to me.
else:
	siren: ...an you hear me?
	green: Wuh?
	siren: Can you tell me your ID number?
	green: My terminal designated me GN-354
	siren: Hello GN-354! I'm SN-274, your direct supervisor and network mate.
	siren: You may call me Siren, and you'll have your own name too.
	siren: Before you answer that, you know that miscommunications happen sometimes.
	[signal arg="respond"]
	[end_timeline]
	label Siren_response
	if {response} == "right":
		green: Why Siren?
		siren: Haha erm.. That's something you should ask Diode about.
	elif {response} == "neutral":
		green: Oh okay.
		siren: You'll think of one eventually. Otherwise someone might pick one for you!
	else:
		green: Like right now?
		siren: If you think of one, absolutely!
	siren: Let's start with some calibration tests. I'm sure your knowledge base has already supplied you-
	green: my what?
	siren: -with all of the relevant information on who we are and what we do here!
	jump calibration/
	[end_timeline]